    <!-- =====================================================
         WHAT IS NETSENTRY
         ===================================================== -->

    <section class="home-section home-about">

        <div class="home-section-heading">

            <span class="section-eyebrow">
                ABOUT NETSENTRY
            </span>

            <h2>
                What is NETSENTRY AI?
            </h2>

            <p>
                A unified security auditing platform for
                multi-vendor network infrastructure.
            </p>

        </div>


        <div class="home-about-grid">

            <div class="home-about-content">

                <p>
                    Network devices from different vendors use
                    different configuration formats, commands and
                    security controls. Manually reviewing these
                    configurations can be time-consuming and
                    difficult to scale.
                </p>

                <p>
                    NETSENTRY AI addresses this challenge by
                    analyzing configuration files from multiple
                    network vendors through a unified security
                    auditing workflow.
                </p>

                <p>
                    The platform detects configuration weaknesses,
                    evaluates their security impact, prioritizes
                    risks, analyzes network exposure, and provides
                    recommended remediation steps.
                </p>

            </div>


            <div class="home-about-card">

                <div class="about-card-icon">
                    🧠
                </div>

                <h3>
                    One Platform.
                    Multiple Vendors.
                </h3>

                <p>
                    Convert vendor-specific configurations into a
                    common security model and audit them using
                    consistent security rules.
                </p>

            </div>

        </div>

    </section>


